<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia says investigating EU dumping charges.</title>
<headline>Indonesia says investigating EU dumping charges.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia said on Tuesday it was investigating dumping charges by the European Union over the country's unbleached cotton fabrics products.</p>
<p>&quot;The government is in the process of investigating dumping charges on imported polyester yarn (in the local market) and charges of dumping by the European Union over (Indonesia's) unbleached cotton fabrics,&quot; Industry and Trade Minister Tungky Ariwibowo said in a statement during a parliamentary hearing.</p>
<p>Ariwibowo also said the government had stepped up measures to prevent smuggling of textiles and textile products into the local market.</p>
<p>He said the government was concerned over recent allegations over smuggling of textile products into the local market which could have a negative impact on the domestic textile industry.</p>
<p>Ariwibowo did not give further details.</p>
<p>Textiles are among Indonesia's most important export products.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
